,title,link,text,language,family
0,Nottoway people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nottoway_people,"The Nottoway are an Iroquoian Native American tribe in Virginia. The Nottoway spoke the Nottoway language, a member of the Iroquoian language family.",Nottoway-Meherrin,Iroquoian
1,Meherrin Native Americans,https://davidarthur.us/MeherrinNativeAmer.htm,"The Nottoway and Meherrin, Iroquoian-speaking tribes, lived along Virginia�s southern border and shared linguistic and cultural ties with the Tuscarora and the Haudenosaunee.",Nottoway-Meherrin,Iroquoian
2,Native North American Tribes - Cheroenhaka / Nottoway,https://www.historyfiles.co.uk/KingListsAmericas/NorthNottoway.htm,"Iroquoian-speaking tribes occupied the lands to the east of the Fall Line on the inner coastal plains of south-eastern Virginia. These tribes included the Cheroenhaka (Nottoway) amongst their number, along with the Meherrin and the Tuscarora.",Nottoway-Meherrin,Iroquoian
3,Nottoway-Meherrin Language (NWY)... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/nwy/,Nottoway-Meherrin is an extinct language of the United States. It belongs to the Iroquoian language family.,Nottoway-Meherrin,Iroquoian
4,Iroquoian languages - Wikiwand,https://www.wikiwand.com/en/Iroquoian_languages,"The Iroquoian languages, occasionally referred to as the Ogwehoweh languages, are a family of indigenous languages of North America. They are known for their general lack of labial consonants.",Nottoway-Meherrin,Iroquoian
5,My heart is at Meherrin Powwow | NC Arts Council,https://www.ncarts.org/blog/2020/12/09/my-heart-meherrin-powwow,"Powwow is where the Meherrin enact the Iroquois ways, to rekindle the fire of allegiance with the Nottoway and the Tuscarora and to gather the community in homecoming.",Nottoway-Meherrin,Iroquoian
6,1711-1725 – Meherrin Indian Nation,https://meherrinnation.org/history-culture/history/1711-1725/,"In 1718, the Nottoway and Meherrin went to the Seneca with a wampum belt, in an offer of peace. This made the Virginia government anxious about “the danger of suffering the Nottoway and Maherine Indians to bring in the said Northern Indians”.",Nottoway-Meherrin,Iroquoian
7,Nottoway language Facts for Kids,https://kids.kiddle.co/Nottoway_language,"nwy Nottoway-Meherrin. Nottoway, also called Cheroenhaka, was a language spoken by the Nottoway people. It is closely related to the Tuscarora language. Both are part of the Iroquoian language family.",Nottoway-Meherrin,Iroquoian
8,"Full text of ""enwiki-Nottoway_language-20200725.pdf""",https://archive.org/stream/enwiki-Nottoway_language-20200725.pdf/enwiki-Nottoway_language-20200725_djvu.txt,"Nottoway-Meherrin.By comparing words in Wood’s vocabulary with cognates in other Iroquoian languages, Blair Rudes (1981) was able to reconstruct the phonemes of Nottoway. According to Rudes (1981: 46), Nottoway has five vowel phonemes as seen in the following table.",Nottoway-Meherrin,Iroquoian
9,Meherrin: People of the Water,https://www.ncpedia.org/printpdf/25777,"The Meherrin, Tuscarora and Nottoway were referred to as Mangoac /Mangoak, a generic term used by the Algonquin Nations to denote Iroquoian speaking people.",Nottoway-Meherrin,Iroquoian
